SCRAPCTL(1)                     SCRAP Tools                    SCRAPCTL(1)

NAME
       scrapctl - manage and observe the Storage Cluster of Repurposed Aging Parts

SYNOPSIS
       scrapctl [COMMAND] [OPTIONS]

DESCRIPTION
       SCRAP is a self-aware storage system designed for drives that
       should have been recycled years ago. It performs dynamic
       redundancy and emotional support for your failing disks.

COMMANDS
       status      Display current array condition.
       rebuild     Attempt to reconstruct data using remaining optimism.
       trust       Show per-drive Trust Score™.
       exorcise    Remove zombie disks that re-mounted themselves.
       therapy     Engage drive in supportive conversation.

EXAMPLES
       scrapctl status
       scrapctl rebuild --force
       scrapctl trust /dev/sdc
       scrapctl exorcise /dev/sdd

FILES
       /etc/scrap.yaml   Primary configuration
       /var/log/scrap/   Event logs and poetry

SEE ALSO
       scrapd(8), fsck(8), prayer(1)

